{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1292509-a-serious-question-about-mage-revised","id":1292509,"title":"A Serious Question About Mage Revised","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-27T09:18:54-08:00","id":1292509,"title":"A Serious Question About Mage Revised","content":"I have a question concerning the mechanics of Mage: The Ascension Revised Edition and how applicable the mechanics are if you invoke Rule Zero and declare that the Avatar Storm never happened?<br /> <br /> I already own Mage 2E and I have zero interest in M20 for a wide variety of reasons (the Disparate Alliance, the convoluted writing, and the renaming of several Traditions) but I also realize that I own Vampire Revised (corebook only) and tomorrow, I am buying the corebooks for Werewolf Revised and Hunter: The Reckoning.<br /> <br /> While I do love Mage 2E, I also want some semblance of mechanical consistency with the WoD games I am bringing with me to this new school I will be attending this spring. I will be living on campus and so I can only pack so many books. I am allowed five books and I have decided on Vampire: The Masquerade, Werewolf: The Apocalypse, Mage: The Ascension, Hunter: The Reckoning, and Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game (I will also bring Senshi: The Merchandising after I copy the text onto a Word Document and print it out, but even when printed, the entirety of Senshi can fit in a small three-ring binder and still leave plenty of space) and I want to have some mechanical consistency.<br /> <br /> I also typically prefer hard copies to PDF's, so while I will bring my laptop (which has a lot of PDF's on it) I will also bring five hard copies, and those are the ones I've chosen (and yes, I know Street Fighter is more in line with 2E mechanics)<br /> <br /> But to get to the heart of the matter, I am curious as to how drastically altered the mechanics are for Mage: The Ascension Revised<br /> <br /> Obviously, I do not like the metaplot and I intend to run the game using my WoD head-canon where the Avatar Storm never happened and never will. But how easy is that to do in Mage mechanically? I've never read Mage Revised, so I don't know.<br /> <br /> How easy is it to run Mage as &quot;Revised Edition Rules, Second Edition Style&quot;? Is it really just a matter of ST fiat and invoking Rule Zero or do you have to do any serious mechanical adjustments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T10:39:26-08:00","id":1292529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1292509-a-serious-question-about-mage-revised#post1292509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How easy is it to run Mage as &quot;Revised Edition Rules, Second Edition Style&quot;? Is it really just a matter of ST fiat and invoking Rule Zero or do you have to do any serious mechanical adjustments?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let's see, from the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Paradox it's more punishing in the sense that you're always gaining it AND loosing it trough frequent backlash. I don't quite remember the numbers as never use them, but it's less of a damocles sword and more like a constant trouble.<br /> <br /> You have the Divide Successes rule that means that you need to divide your Arete successes between targets and duration. So, for instance, if I cast a fireball to hit 2 targets and manage to get 4 successes , I have 2 successes on damage and 2 are spent on the targets (one for each) for a total of 5 damage each (2 x 2 +1 because Forces adds 1 to the final damage in Revised)<br /> <br /> I think these two are the most notorious changes. So revised magic<s>k</s> takes sligthly more time to cast and has more frequent Paradox backlashes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-27-2019, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:38:58-08:00","id":1292552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1292509-a-serious-question-about-mage-revised?p=1292529#post1292529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, let's see, from the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Paradox it's more punishing in the sense that you're always gaining it AND loosing it trough frequent backlash. I don't quite remember the numbers as never use them, but it's less of a damocles sword and more like a constant trouble.<br /> <br /> You have the Divide Successes rule that means that you need to divide your Arete successes between targets and duration. So, for instance, if I cast a fireball to hit 2 targets and manage to get 4 successes , I have 2 successes on damage and 2 are spent on the targets (one for each) for a total of 5 damage each (2 x 2 +1 because Forces adds 1 to the final damage in Revised)<br /> <br /> I think these two are the most notorious changes. So revised magic<s>k</s> takes sligthly more time to cast and has more frequent Paradox backlashes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T13:10:47-08:00","id":1292583,"title":"","content":"The reason for the changes to Paradox was that MRev alters the way botches work, making them far more rare than they were in 2e. So they rejiggered Paradox to be less dependent on botches. Other than that, you could probably use 2e's Paradox rules without a problem. <br /> <br /> The Splitting Successes thing was done as a way of giving mages more fine control over their castings. But yes, it resulted in castings generally requiring more rolls. If you want to offset this, consider giving mages larger dice pools: Arete+Sphere is a popular option. <br /> <br /> The other big mechanical changes involved Resonance and Quiet: MRev put Resonance dots on the character sheet to give Resonance more prominence in the game; but it didn't handle the rules for how Resonance works terribly well. It's easy enough to ignore Resonance if you wish. <br /> <br /> Quiet got split into three kinds: Madness (which was essentially the same as 2e's Quiet), Clarity (which M20 renamed as Denial), and Jhor (which M20 renamed as Morbidity). Resonance also got three kinds. The idea was that the three types of Resonance and the three kinds of Quiet correspond to the three aspects of the metaphysical trinity: Dynamic Resonance and Madness correspond to Dynamism, Static Resonance and Clarity(/Denial) correspond to Stasis, and Entropic Resonance and Jhor(/Morbidity) correspond to Entropy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T13:31:34-08:00","id":1293134,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer a mix of rules and I'm not sure sometimes where one ended and one began between 2E, Revised, and even Sorcerer's Crusade. If I had to guess on the specifics, we started playing with Revised, but gradually adopted more and more 2E rules and stuff from Sorcerer's Crusade; largely using the mechanics from 2E for magick and Revised for most other things. <br /> <br /> However, sphere descriptions were largely better explained in Revised.<br /> <br /> There's also the split action and damage rules that vary considerably from 2E. <br /> <br /> Given your book limit, I'd probably bring a physical copy of 2E, since that is largely going to be the setting you're using, and just keep a PDF copy of Revised if you want to bring over their mechanics. If your recruiting new people and you want to hand them a book to read, they're going to be confused if you hand them Revised and then say the Avatar Storm and the Ascension War ending hasn't occurred, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 03-01-2019, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T12:04:07-08:00","id":1295367,"title":"","content":"The Traditions aren't really renamed in M20; M20 presents a version of the metaplot where the new Council revise their names to make more sense. The main Sons of Ether writeup has Sons of Ether in big fancy Edwardian font.<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance exists rather contextually (it's only there if the Crafts have gotten the impression that the Technocracy is ruled by the Nephandi), and takes up a tiny proportion of the page-count. The writeup for each Craft is about the Craft itself; you can take absolutely everything from M20 and just say &quot;yeah going to ignore that the Crafts are allied with eachother&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T12:09:01-08:00","id":1295368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1292509-a-serious-question-about-mage-revised?p=1292583#post1292583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity (which M20 renamed as Denial)</div> </div> </div> </div>And that was a very good decision; there is no &quot;clarity&quot; in only seeing your own viewpoint and blinkering out everything else. Denial is more fitting; the idea that you become completely fixed on your own viewpoint and lose the ability to even perceive data that contradicts you. The idea of Technocrats slowly going insane at their desk while no one notices is very creepy and fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}